# Project context

This personal portfolio and journal uses Astro 7, TypeScript, MDX, Tailwind CSS 4,
and Geist fonts. Native Astro templates render static HTML; small browser scripts
handle subscriptions, copying/sharing, and the Orthodox cross canvas. Avoid adding
React or Next.js to the application.

- `src/pages`: pages, journal routes, feeds, metadata endpoints, and server APIs.
- `src/layouts/SiteLayout.astro`: shared layout, metadata, navigation and background.
- `src/components`: Astro UI and web/email MDX renderers.
- `src/content/journal`: MDX content with `title`, `publishedAt`, `summary`, optional
  `image`, and optional `draft`. Drafts are excluded from all published routes.
- `src/lib`: shared constants, content access, UTC date formatting, feed generation,
  and server-only Kit integration. Never expose Kit credentials in browser code.
- `src/styles/global.css`: Tailwind, typography, colors and interaction styles.
- `astro.config.mjs` and `vercel.json`: Astro/Vercel build, redirects and daily cron.

Production is https://alec.wantoch.com and follows `main`. Preserve existing public
URLs and the design. The cross animation retains the original hues, breathing,
swirl, and opacity; respect reduced-motion preferences and clean up listeners.

Run `pnpm check`, `pnpm test`, and `pnpm build` for changes. Use
`node scripts/smoke.mjs <origin>` for route checks. Tests must mock Kit writes;
do not create real subscriptions or broadcasts as part of verification.

Keep secrets in ignored local environment files or Vercel environment variables.
Server functions use `KIT_API_KEY` and `CRON_SECRET`. Public configuration uses
`PUBLIC_BASE_URL` and `PUBLIC_GA_ID` with legacy `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` compatibility.
Use ASCII in YAML frontmatter, configuration, file paths, and shell commands.
